{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KH2aF8Qc4adiLYLmC7JeTf","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a comprehensive understanding of the codebase. Let me create a detailed summary:\n\n## Codebase Exploration Summary\n\nI've thoroughly analyzed the Roundnet project's authentication setup, user registration, form components, and i18n configuration. Here's a comprehensive overview:\n\n---\n\n## 1. SUPABASE CONFIGURATION\n\n**File:** `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/src/lib/supabase.ts`\n\nThe Supabase client is initialized with environment variables and exported as a singleton:\n\n```typescript\nimport { createClient } from '@supabase/supabase-js'\n\nconst supabaseUrl = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL\nconst supabaseAnonKey = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY\n\nexport const supabase = createClient(supabaseUrl, supabaseAnonKey)\n```\n\n**Key Points:**\n- Uses public environment variables for client-side initialization\n- Requires `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` and `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`\n- Version: `^2.93.3` (from package.json)\n\n---\n\n## 2. USER REGISTRATION IMPLEMENTATION\n\n**File:** `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/src/components/registration-form.tsx`\n\n**Architecture:**\n- Uses `react-hook-form` with Zod validation\n- Full Name acts as the username (stored in Supabase auth user metadata as `full_name`)\n- Real-time username availability checking with debounce (500ms)\n- Email is optional; if not provided, a placeholder email is generated\n\n**Username Storage Pattern:**\n```typescript\n// Line 88-92: Checking availability against the profiles table\nconst { data, error } = await supabase\n  .from(\"profiles\")\n  .select(\"full_name\")\n  .ilike(\"full_name\", username)  // Case-insensitive search\n  .maybeSingle();\n\n// Line 145: Generating placeholder email if none provided\nemail: values.email || `${values.fullName.toLowerCase().replace(/\\s+/g, \"_\")}@placeholder.local`\n\n// Line 148-150: Storing full_name in user metadata\noptions: {\n  data: {\n    full_name: values.fullName,\n  },\n  emailRedirectTo: values.email ? `${window.location.origin}/auth/callback` : undefined,\n}\n```\n\n**Form Validation Schema (Dynamic):**\n```typescript\nconst createRegistrationSchema = (t) =>\n  z.object({\n    fullName: z.string()\n      .min(1, t(\"errors.fullNameRequired\"))\n      .min(2, t(\"errors.fullNameMinLength\"))\n      .max(100, t(\"errors.fullNameMaxLength\")),\n    email: z.string()\n      .email(t(\"errors.emailInvalid\"))\n      .optional()\n      .or(z.literal(\"\")),\n    password: z.string()\n      .min(1, t(\"errors.passwordRequired\"))\n      .min(8, t(\"errors.passwordMinLength\")),\n    confirmPassword: z.string(),\n  })\n  .refine((data) => data.password === data.confirmPassword, {\n    message: t(\"errors.passwordsDoNotMatch\"),\n    path: [\"confirmPassword\"],\n  });\n```\n\n**Username Availability Features:**\n- Real-time validation with visual feedback (CheckCircle, XCircle, Loader2 icons)\n- States: \"idle\" → \"checking\" → \"available\"/\"taken\"\n- Debounced API call (500ms) to prevent excessive queries\n- Submit button disabled when username is \"taken\" or \"checking\"\n\n---\n\n## 3. FORM COMPONENTS & PATTERNS\n\n**UI Components Located in:** `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/src/components/ui/`\n\n### Form Component (`form.tsx`)\n- Built on `react-hook-form` with Radix UI and custom context\n- Components: `Form`, `FormField`, `FormItem`, `FormLabel`, `FormControl`, `FormDescription`, `FormMessage`\n- Provides form state management with proper error handling\n- Accessible with ARIA attributes (`aria-describedby`, `aria-invalid`)\n\n### Input Component (`input.tsx`)\n- Native HTML input with Tailwind styling\n- Supports custom className merging\n- Accessible focus states and validation states\n\n### Button Component (`button.tsx`)\n- Built with CVA (Class Variance Authority)\n- Variants: `default`, `destructive`, `outline`, `secondary`, `ghost`, `link`\n- Sizes: `default`, `xs`, `sm`, `lg`, `icon`, `icon-xs`, `icon-sm`, `icon-lg`\n- Disabled state handling and focus-visible styling\n\n### Label Component (`label.tsx`)\n- Wrapper around Radix UI Label\n- Supports disabled state through data attributes\n- Accessible peer-disabled states\n\n---\n\n## 4. INTERNATIONALIZATION (i18n) SETUP\n\n**Files:**\n- Config: `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/src/i18n/config.ts`\n- Request: `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/src/i18n/request.ts`\n- Routing: `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/src/i18n/routing.ts`\n\n**Configuration:**\n```typescript\n// config.ts\nexport const locales = ['es', 'en'] as const;\nexport const defaultLocale = 'es' as const;\n\n// routing.ts\nexport const routing = defineRouting({\n  locales,\n  defaultLocale,\n});\n\n// request.ts - Loads translations dynamically\nexport default getRequestConfig(async ({ requestLocale }) => {\n  let locale = await requestLocale;\n  if (!locale || !routing.locales.includes(locale)) {\n    locale = routing.defaultLocale;\n  }\n  return {\n    locale,\n    messages: (await import(`../../messages/${locale}.json`)).default,\n  };\n});\n```\n\n**Middleware:** `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/src/middleware.ts`\n```typescript\nexport default createMiddleware(routing);\nexport const config = {\n  matcher: ['/((?!api|auth|_next|_vercel|.*\\\\..*).*)',],\n};\n```\n\n**Message Files:**\n\n**English** (`/messages/en.json`):\n```json\n{\n  \"registration\": {\n    \"title\": \"Create your account\",\n    \"subtitle\": \"Join Roundnet Spain\",\n    \"fullName\": \"Full Name\",\n    \"fullNamePlaceholder\": \"Enter your full name\",\n    \"fullNameDescription\": \"This will be your unique username on the platform\",\n    \"email\": \"Email (optional)\",\n    \"password\": \"Password\",\n    \"passwordDescription\": \"Minimum 8 characters\",\n    \"confirmPassword\": \"Confirm Password\",\n    \"submit\": \"Create Account\",\n    \"submitting\": \"Creating account...\",\n    \"success\": \"Account created successfully!\",\n    \"successWithEmail\": \"Account created! Please check your email to verify your account.\",\n    \"errors\": {\n      \"fullNameRequired\": \"Full name is required\",\n      \"fullNameMinLength\": \"Full name must be at least 2 characters\",\n      \"fullNameMaxLength\": \"Full name must be less than 100 characters\",\n      \"fullNameTaken\": \"This name is already taken\",\n      \"fullNameChecking\": \"Checking availability...\",\n      \"fullNameAvailable\": \"This name is available\",\n      \"emailInvalid\": \"Please enter a valid email address\",\n      \"passwordRequired\": \"Password is required\",\n      \"passwordMinLength\": \"Password must be at least 8 characters\",\n      \"passwordsDoNotMatch\": \"Passwords do not match\",\n      \"registrationFailed\": \"Registration failed. Please try again.\",\n      \"genericError\": \"An error occurred. Please try again.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"auth\": {\n    \"login\": \"Log in\",\n    \"logout\": \"Log out\",\n    \"profile\": \"Profile\",\n    \"account\": \"Account\",\n    \"register\": \"Register\",\n    \"alreadyHaveAccount\": \"Already have an account?\",\n    \"noAccount\": \"Don't have an account?\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Spanish** (`/messages/es.json`): Same structure with Spanish translations\n\n**Usage Pattern:**\n```typescript\nconst t = useTranslations(\"registration\");\n// t(\"title\") → \"Create your account\" (en) or \"Crea tu cuenta\" (es)\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. AUTHENTICATION PAGES & COMPONENTS\n\n### Registration Page Structure\n\n**Route:** `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/src/app/[locale]/register/page.tsx`\n```typescript\nexport default async function RegisterPage({\n  params,\n}: {\n  params: Promise<{ locale: string }>;\n}) {\n  const { locale } = await params;\n  setRequestLocale(locale);\n  return <RegisterPageContent />;\n}\n```\n\n**Content Component:** `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/src/app/[locale]/register/register-content.tsx`\n```typescript\nexport function RegisterPageContent() {\n  const t = useTranslations(\"registration\");\n  const tAuth = useTranslations(\"auth\");\n  const locale = useLocale();\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"flex min-h-[calc(100vh-8rem)] items-center justify-center px-4 py-12\">\n      <div className=\"w-full max-w-md space-y-8\">\n        <div className=\"text-center\">\n          <h1 className=\"text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight\">{t(\"title\")}</h1>\n          <p className=\"mt-2 text-muted-foreground\">{t(\"subtitle\")}</p>\n        </div>\n        <div className=\"rounded-lg border bg-card p-6 shadow-sm\">\n          <RegistrationForm />\n        </div>\n        <p className=\"text-center text-sm text-muted-foreground\">\n          {tAuth(\"alreadyHaveAccount\")}{\" \"}\n          <Link href={`/${locale}/login`} className=\"font-medium text-primary hover:underline\">\n            {tAuth(\"login\")}\n          </Link>\n        </p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### Auth Callback Route\n\n**File:** `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/src/app/auth/callback/route.ts`\n```typescript\nexport async function GET(request: NextRequest) {\n  const requestUrl = new URL(request.url);\n  const code = requestUrl.searchParams.get(\"code\");\n  const origin = requestUrl.origin;\n\n  if (code) {\n    const { error } = await supabase.auth.exchangeCodeForSession(code);\n    if (error) {\n      console.error(\"Auth callback error:\", error);\n      return NextResponse.redirect(`${origin}/es?error=auth_callback_failed`);\n    }\n  }\n  return NextResponse.redirect(`${origin}/es`);\n}\n```\n\n### Username Availability Check API\n\n**File:** `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/src/app/api/auth/check-username/route.ts`\n```typescript\nexport async function GET(request: Request) {\n  const { searchParams } = new URL(request.url);\n  const username = searchParams.get(\"username\");\n\n  if (!username || username.length < 2) {\n    return NextResponse.json({ error: \"...\" }, { status: 400 });\n  }\n\n  try {\n    const { data, error } = await supabase\n      .from(\"profiles\")\n      .select(\"full_name\")\n      .ilike(\"full_name\", username)\n      .maybeSingle();\n\n    if (error && error.code === \"42P01\") {\n      // Table doesn't exist yet, treat as available\n      return NextResponse.json({ available: true });\n    }\n\n    return NextResponse.json({ available: !data });\n  } catch (error) {\n    return NextResponse.json(\n      { error: \"Failed to check username availability\" },\n      { status: 500 }\n    );\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. LAYOUT & LOCALIZATION\n\n**Main Layout:** `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/src/app/[locale]/layout.tsx`\n\n**Key Features:**\n- Server-side locale validation and setting\n- Dynamic metadata generation based on locale\n- NextIntlClientProvider wrapping all children\n- Header and Footer components included\n- Geist fonts loaded from Google Fonts\n- Static param generation for all locales\n\n```typescript\nexport function generateStaticParams() {\n  return routing.locales.map((locale) => ({ locale }));\n}\n\nexport async function generateMetadata({\n  params,\n}: {\n  params: Promise<{ locale: string }>;\n}): Promise<Metadata> {\n  const { locale } = await params;\n  const messages = await getMessages({ locale });\n  const metadata = messages.metadata as { title: string; description: string };\n  return {\n    title: metadata.title,\n    description: metadata.description,\n  };\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. PROJECT DEPENDENCIES\n\n**Key Libraries:**\n- `@supabase/supabase-js`: ^2.93.3 - Backend & authentication\n- `next-intl`: ^4.8.2 - Internationalization\n- `react-hook-form`: ^7.71.1 - Form state management\n- `zod`: ^4.3.6 - Schema validation\n- `@hookform/resolvers`: ^5.2.2 - Validation resolver\n- `radix-ui`: ^1.4.3 - Unstyled accessible UI primitives\n- `lucide-react`: ^0.563.0 - Icon library\n- `tailwindcss`: ^4 - CSS framework\n\n---\n\n## 8. TRANSLATION ERROR MESSAGES PATTERN\n\nThe i18n setup allows for nested translation keys and dynamic schema validation:\n\n**For Login (when implemented):**\n- Namespace: `auth` with keys: `login`, `logout`, `profile`, `account`, `register`, `alreadyHaveAccount`, `noAccount`\n\n**For Registration:**\n- Namespace: `registration` with keys organized by:\n  - Form fields: `fullName`, `email`, `password`, `confirmPassword`\n  - Descriptions & placeholders\n  - Success messages: `success`, `successWithEmail`\n  - Error messages under `errors.*`\n\n---\n\n## 9. VALIDATION PATTERNS\n\n**Schema is created dynamically** to access translations:\n```typescript\nconst createRegistrationSchema = (t: ReturnType<typeof useTranslations>) => \n  z.object({ ... })\n```\n\nThis allows:\n- Real-time i18n-aware validation messages\n- Client-side validation feedback\n- Error display in user's selected language\n\n**Error Handling:**\n- Zod schema validation → form field errors\n- Manual form errors for username conflicts\n- Submit error messages for registration failures\n- Success messages with conditional content based on email presence\n\n---\n\n## 10. NEXT.JS CONFIGURATION\n\n**File:** `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/next.config.ts`\n\n```typescript\nimport createNextIntlPlugin from \"next-intl/plugin\";\nconst withNextIntl = createNextIntlPlugin(\"./src/i18n/request.ts\");\n\nconst nextConfig: NextConfig = {\n  /* config options here */\n};\n\nexport default withNextIntl(nextConfig);\n```\n\n---\n\n## Summary of Key Patterns\n\n1. **Authentication Flow:** Email signup with Supabase, username (full_name) as unique identifier\n2. **Form Validation:** Client-side with Zod + React Hook Form, i18n-aware error messages\n3. **Username Management:** Full name stored as username, checked via Supabase profiles table with case-insensitive ILIKE query\n4. **Real-time Feedback:** Debounced availability checking with visual status indicators\n5. **i18n Strategy:** next-intl with JSON message files, locale in URL params, server-side validation & client-side usage\n6. **Component Architecture:** Headless UI primitives (Radix UI) + Tailwind styling + CVA for variants\n7. **Error Handling:** Multi-level (schema, manual, submission) with translated messages"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a9e90a5 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6fb93add-4f2d-45be-b50f-ea5a97535704","uuid":"dabcdba5-a1ca-4355-83a9-91ad6e8fe0ad","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Explore the codebase to understand:\n1. Current authentication setup (Supabase client, auth utilities)\n2. User registration implementation (how usernames are stored)\n3. Existing form components and patterns\n4. i18n/translation setup for error messages\n5. Any existing login page or auth components\n\nFocus on files related to:\n- Supabase configuration\n- Auth utilities\n- User registration page\n- Form components\n- i18n translations\n\nProvide a thorough summary of the relevant files and patterns used.","agentId":"a9e90a5","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a comprehensive understanding of the codebase. Let me create a detailed summary:\n\n## Codebase Exploration Summary\n\nI've thoroughly analyzed the Roundnet project's authentication setup, user registration, form components, and i18n configuration. Here's a comprehensive overview:\n\n---\n\n## 1. SUPABASE CONFIGURATION\n\n**File:** `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/src/lib/supabase.ts`\n\nThe Supabase client is initialized with environment variables and exported as a singleton:\n\n```typescript\nimport { createClient } from '@supabase/supabase-js'\n\nconst supabaseUrl = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL\nconst supabaseAnonKey = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY\n\nexport const supabase = createClient(supabaseUrl, supabaseAnonKey)\n```\n\n**Key Points:**\n- Uses public environment variables for client-side initialization\n- Requires `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` and `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`\n- Version: `^2.93.3` (from package.json)\n\n---\n\n## 2. USER REGISTRATION IMPLEMENTATION\n\n**File:** `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/src/components/registration-form.tsx`\n\n**Architecture:**\n- Uses `react-hook-form` with Zod validation\n- Full Name acts as the username (stored in Supabase auth user metadata as `full_name`)\n- Real-time username availability checking with debounce (500ms)\n- Email is optional; if not provided, a placeholder email is generated\n\n**Username Storage Pattern:**\n```typescript\n// Line 88-92: Checking availability against the profiles table\nconst { data, error } = await supabase\n  .from(\"profiles\")\n  .select(\"full_name\")\n  .ilike(\"full_name\", username)  // Case-insensitive search\n  .maybeSingle();\n\n// Line 145: Generating placeholder email if none provided\nemail: values.email || `${values.fullName.toLowerCase().replace(/\\s+/g, \"_\")}@placeholder.local`\n\n// Line 148-150: Storing full_name in user metadata\noptions: {\n  data: {\n    full_name: values.fullName,\n  },\n  emailRedirectTo: values.email ? `${window.location.origin}/auth/callback` : undefined,\n}\n```\n\n**Form Validation Schema (Dynamic):**\n```typescript\nconst createRegistrationSchema = (t) =>\n  z.object({\n    fullName: z.string()\n      .min(1, t(\"errors.fullNameRequired\"))\n      .min(2, t(\"errors.fullNameMinLength\"))\n      .max(100, t(\"errors.fullNameMaxLength\")),\n    email: z.string()\n      .email(t(\"errors.emailInvalid\"))\n      .optional()\n      .or(z.literal(\"\")),\n    password: z.string()\n      .min(1, t(\"errors.passwordRequired\"))\n      .min(8, t(\"errors.passwordMinLength\")),\n    confirmPassword: z.string(),\n  })\n  .refine((data) => data.password === data.confirmPassword, {\n    message: t(\"errors.passwordsDoNotMatch\"),\n    path: [\"confirmPassword\"],\n  });\n```\n\n**Username Availability Features:**\n- Real-time validation with visual feedback (CheckCircle, XCircle, Loader2 icons)\n- States: \"idle\" → \"checking\" → \"available\"/\"taken\"\n- Debounced API call (500ms) to prevent excessive queries\n- Submit button disabled when username is \"taken\" or \"checking\"\n\n---\n\n## 3. FORM COMPONENTS & PATTERNS\n\n**UI Components Located in:** `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/src/components/ui/`\n\n### Form Component (`form.tsx`)\n- Built on `react-hook-form` with Radix UI and custom context\n- Components: `Form`, `FormField`, `FormItem`, `FormLabel`, `FormControl`, `FormDescription`, `FormMessage`\n- Provides form state management with proper error handling\n- Accessible with ARIA attributes (`aria-describedby`, `aria-invalid`)\n\n### Input Component (`input.tsx`)\n- Native HTML input with Tailwind styling\n- Supports custom className merging\n- Accessible focus states and validation states\n\n### Button Component (`button.tsx`)\n- Built with CVA (Class Variance Authority)\n- Variants: `default`, `destructive`, `outline`, `secondary`, `ghost`, `link`\n- Sizes: `default`, `xs`, `sm`, `lg`, `icon`, `icon-xs`, `icon-sm`, `icon-lg`\n- Disabled state handling and focus-visible styling\n\n### Label Component (`label.tsx`)\n- Wrapper around Radix UI Label\n- Supports disabled state through data attributes\n- Accessible peer-disabled states\n\n---\n\n## 4. INTERNATIONALIZATION (i18n) SETUP\n\n**Files:**\n- Config: `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/src/i18n/config.ts`\n- Request: `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/src/i18n/request.ts`\n- Routing: `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/src/i18n/routing.ts`\n\n**Configuration:**\n```typescript\n// config.ts\nexport const locales = ['es', 'en'] as const;\nexport const defaultLocale = 'es' as const;\n\n// routing.ts\nexport const routing = defineRouting({\n  locales,\n  defaultLocale,\n});\n\n// request.ts - Loads translations dynamically\nexport default getRequestConfig(async ({ requestLocale }) => {\n  let locale = await requestLocale;\n  if (!locale || !routing.locales.includes(locale)) {\n    locale = routing.defaultLocale;\n  }\n  return {\n    locale,\n    messages: (await import(`../../messages/${locale}.json`)).default,\n  };\n});\n```\n\n**Middleware:** `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/src/middleware.ts`\n```typescript\nexport default createMiddleware(routing);\nexport const config = {\n  matcher: ['/((?!api|auth|_next|_vercel|.*\\\\..*).*)',],\n};\n```\n\n**Message Files:**\n\n**English** (`/messages/en.json`):\n```json\n{\n  \"registration\": {\n    \"title\": \"Create your account\",\n    \"subtitle\": \"Join Roundnet Spain\",\n    \"fullName\": \"Full Name\",\n    \"fullNamePlaceholder\": \"Enter your full name\",\n    \"fullNameDescription\": \"This will be your unique username on the platform\",\n    \"email\": \"Email (optional)\",\n    \"password\": \"Password\",\n    \"passwordDescription\": \"Minimum 8 characters\",\n    \"confirmPassword\": \"Confirm Password\",\n    \"submit\": \"Create Account\",\n    \"submitting\": \"Creating account...\",\n    \"success\": \"Account created successfully!\",\n    \"successWithEmail\": \"Account created! Please check your email to verify your account.\",\n    \"errors\": {\n      \"fullNameRequired\": \"Full name is required\",\n      \"fullNameMinLength\": \"Full name must be at least 2 characters\",\n      \"fullNameMaxLength\": \"Full name must be less than 100 characters\",\n      \"fullNameTaken\": \"This name is already taken\",\n      \"fullNameChecking\": \"Checking availability...\",\n      \"fullNameAvailable\": \"This name is available\",\n      \"emailInvalid\": \"Please enter a valid email address\",\n      \"passwordRequired\": \"Password is required\",\n      \"passwordMinLength\": \"Password must be at least 8 characters\",\n      \"passwordsDoNotMatch\": \"Passwords do not match\",\n      \"registrationFailed\": \"Registration failed. Please try again.\",\n      \"genericError\": \"An error occurred. Please try again.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"auth\": {\n    \"login\": \"Log in\",\n    \"logout\": \"Log out\",\n    \"profile\": \"Profile\",\n    \"account\": \"Account\",\n    \"register\": \"Register\",\n    \"alreadyHaveAccount\": \"Already have an account?\",\n    \"noAccount\": \"Don't have an account?\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Spanish** (`/messages/es.json`): Same structure with Spanish translations\n\n**Usage Pattern:**\n```typescript\nconst t = useTranslations(\"registration\");\n// t(\"title\") → \"Create your account\" (en) or \"Crea tu cuenta\" (es)\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. AUTHENTICATION PAGES & COMPONENTS\n\n### Registration Page Structure\n\n**Route:** `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/src/app/[locale]/register/page.tsx`\n```typescript\nexport default async function RegisterPage({\n  params,\n}: {\n  params: Promise<{ locale: string }>;\n}) {\n  const { locale } = await params;\n  setRequestLocale(locale);\n  return <RegisterPageContent />;\n}\n```\n\n**Content Component:** `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/src/app/[locale]/register/register-content.tsx`\n```typescript\nexport function RegisterPageContent() {\n  const t = useTranslations(\"registration\");\n  const tAuth = useTranslations(\"auth\");\n  const locale = useLocale();\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"flex min-h-[calc(100vh-8rem)] items-center justify-center px-4 py-12\">\n      <div className=\"w-full max-w-md space-y-8\">\n        <div className=\"text-center\">\n          <h1 className=\"text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight\">{t(\"title\")}</h1>\n          <p className=\"mt-2 text-muted-foreground\">{t(\"subtitle\")}</p>\n        </div>\n        <div className=\"rounded-lg border bg-card p-6 shadow-sm\">\n          <RegistrationForm />\n        </div>\n        <p className=\"text-center text-sm text-muted-foreground\">\n          {tAuth(\"alreadyHaveAccount\")}{\" \"}\n          <Link href={`/${locale}/login`} className=\"font-medium text-primary hover:underline\">\n            {tAuth(\"login\")}\n          </Link>\n        </p>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### Auth Callback Route\n\n**File:** `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/src/app/auth/callback/route.ts`\n```typescript\nexport async function GET(request: NextRequest) {\n  const requestUrl = new URL(request.url);\n  const code = requestUrl.searchParams.get(\"code\");\n  const origin = requestUrl.origin;\n\n  if (code) {\n    const { error } = await supabase.auth.exchangeCodeForSession(code);\n    if (error) {\n      console.error(\"Auth callback error:\", error);\n      return NextResponse.redirect(`${origin}/es?error=auth_callback_failed`);\n    }\n  }\n  return NextResponse.redirect(`${origin}/es`);\n}\n```\n\n### Username Availability Check API\n\n**File:** `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/src/app/api/auth/check-username/route.ts`\n```typescript\nexport async function GET(request: Request) {\n  const { searchParams } = new URL(request.url);\n  const username = searchParams.get(\"username\");\n\n  if (!username || username.length < 2) {\n    return NextResponse.json({ error: \"...\" }, { status: 400 });\n  }\n\n  try {\n    const { data, error } = await supabase\n      .from(\"profiles\")\n      .select(\"full_name\")\n      .ilike(\"full_name\", username)\n      .maybeSingle();\n\n    if (error && error.code === \"42P01\") {\n      // Table doesn't exist yet, treat as available\n      return NextResponse.json({ available: true });\n    }\n\n    return NextResponse.json({ available: !data });\n  } catch (error) {\n    return NextResponse.json(\n      { error: \"Failed to check username availability\" },\n      { status: 500 }\n    );\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. LAYOUT & LOCALIZATION\n\n**Main Layout:** `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/src/app/[locale]/layout.tsx`\n\n**Key Features:**\n- Server-side locale validation and setting\n- Dynamic metadata generation based on locale\n- NextIntlClientProvider wrapping all children\n- Header and Footer components included\n- Geist fonts loaded from Google Fonts\n- Static param generation for all locales\n\n```typescript\nexport function generateStaticParams() {\n  return routing.locales.map((locale) => ({ locale }));\n}\n\nexport async function generateMetadata({\n  params,\n}: {\n  params: Promise<{ locale: string }>;\n}): Promise<Metadata> {\n  const { locale } = await params;\n  const messages = await getMessages({ locale });\n  const metadata = messages.metadata as { title: string; description: string };\n  return {\n    title: metadata.title,\n    description: metadata.description,\n  };\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. PROJECT DEPENDENCIES\n\n**Key Libraries:**\n- `@supabase/supabase-js`: ^2.93.3 - Backend & authentication\n- `next-intl`: ^4.8.2 - Internationalization\n- `react-hook-form`: ^7.71.1 - Form state management\n- `zod`: ^4.3.6 - Schema validation\n- `@hookform/resolvers`: ^5.2.2 - Validation resolver\n- `radix-ui`: ^1.4.3 - Unstyled accessible UI primitives\n- `lucide-react`: ^0.563.0 - Icon library\n- `tailwindcss`: ^4 - CSS framework\n\n---\n\n## 8. TRANSLATION ERROR MESSAGES PATTERN\n\nThe i18n setup allows for nested translation keys and dynamic schema validation:\n\n**For Login (when implemented):**\n- Namespace: `auth` with keys: `login`, `logout`, `profile`, `account`, `register`, `alreadyHaveAccount`, `noAccount`\n\n**For Registration:**\n- Namespace: `registration` with keys organized by:\n  - Form fields: `fullName`, `email`, `password`, `confirmPassword`\n  - Descriptions & placeholders\n  - Success messages: `success`, `successWithEmail`\n  - Error messages under `errors.*`\n\n---\n\n## 9. VALIDATION PATTERNS\n\n**Schema is created dynamically** to access translations:\n```typescript\nconst createRegistrationSchema = (t: ReturnType<typeof useTranslations>) => \n  z.object({ ... })\n```\n\nThis allows:\n- Real-time i18n-aware validation messages\n- Client-side validation feedback\n- Error display in user's selected language\n\n**Error Handling:**\n- Zod schema validation → form field errors\n- Manual form errors for username conflicts\n- Submit error messages for registration failures\n- Success messages with conditional content based on email presence\n\n---\n\n## 10. NEXT.JS CONFIGURATION\n\n**File:** `/Users/anayusta/workspace/roundnet/next.config.ts`\n\n```typescript\nimport createNextIntlPlugin from \"next-intl/plugin\";\nconst withNextIntl = createNextIntlPlugin(\"./src/i18n/request.ts\");\n\nconst nextConfig: NextConfig = {\n  /* config options here */\n};\n\nexport default withNextIntl(nextConfig);\n```\n\n---\n\n## Summary of Key Patterns\n\n1. **Authentication Flow:** Email signup with Supabase, username (full_name) as unique identifier\n2. **Form Validation:** Client-side with Zod + React Hook Form, i18n-aware error messages\n3. **Username Management:** Full name stored as username, checked via Supabase profiles table with case-insensitive ILIKE query\n4. **Real-time Feedback:** Debounced availability checking with visual status indicators\n5. **i18n Strategy:** next-intl with JSON message files, locale in URL params, server-side validation & client-side usage\n6. **Component Architecture:** Headless UI primitives (Radix UI) + Tailwind styling + CVA for variants\n7. **Error Handling:** Multi-level (schema, manual, submission) with translated messages"}],"totalDurationMs":55622,"totalTokens":73905,"totalToolUseCount":34,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":937,"cache_read_input_tokens":72960,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":937},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"}}}
